      "views": [
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "**PanicButton** triggers a true kernel panic from Settings. The phone reboots immediately and a full `panic-full` log is saved to Settings > Privacy > Analytics.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Read this first"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "- The phone **reboots immediately**. Save anything open.\n- Dopamine is semi-untethered, so you boot to stock. Re-jailbreak afterwards.\n- No data is lost. iOS journals the filesystem.\n- Works while jailbroken with Dopamine (rootless).",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "How it works"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "1. You tap **Trigger Kernel Panic** in Settings.\n2. SpringBoard shows a system alert asking you to confirm.\n3. A suid-root helper calls `reboot` with `RB_PANIC`, the kernel's own debug panic.\n\nThe panic log is a normal `panic-full` log with the full backtrace. Nothing is written to kernel memory.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "How to use"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "1. Install PanicButton from Cobalt.\n2. Open Settings > PanicButton.\n3. Tap **Trigger Kernel Panic** and confirm.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
